# what the linked compiler frontend needs from the thread it runs on
#
# mls compiles the compiler's own frontend into itself and runs it on the
# analysis thread and the rebuild worker. The compiler sizes the stack that
# frontend runs on in its manifest: the parser descends MAX_NEST_DEPTH levels
# before it refuses, 8.2 MiB of win64 frames, and the compiler reserves twice
# that (dep/mach/mach.toml, mach#3325). A thread spawned with std's 2 MiB
# default runs the same recursion on a quarter of that, and the first input
# deep enough kills the process with nothing on stderr (#345). A reserve is
# address space, not memory, so holding the compiler's bound costs nothing
# until the frontend actually uses it.

use std.types.size.usize;

# the stack reserve of every thread that runs the linked frontend, in bytes
pub val STACK_RESERVE: usize = 0x1000000;
